            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "NOTE 2 One example for a higher priority grid code requirement would arise from the fact that asymmetry limits typically apply to the grid connection point. So if the energy management of the building sees extreme asymmetries it might compensate them. In the ISO 15118 series this would be communicated via phase specific EVSETargetActivePower(_L2/L3) values, which would override the default behavior defined in the MaximumPowerAsymmetry.",
